  mean held-out accuracy
    B1 association       1.000   <- the milestone
    B1, rate divided out 0.760
    B1, labels shuffled  0.400   (the control: must sit at chance)
    B3 vision            1.000   (the input module; plumbing, not the claim)
    at or above 0.75     5 of 5 creatures

  M2 PASS — a held-out classifier reads object-present from B1 at 100%
  (chance 50%, shuffled control 40%). With each trial's overall firing
  rate divided out it still reads 76%, so most of what B1 carries about
  the object is how hard it is working and some of it is where.
