    against 0.371 through the nine motor groups. Same estimator,
    same trials, same split; the only change is which vector a
    trial is. The module does NOT hold what the knobs miss, so the
    ceiling is upstream of the larynx, not in its
    parameterisation.

  one of eight on the ARTICULATORS: 0.344 (chance 0.125)
    <- THE CLAIM. Drops loudness and voicing, which the row below
    does not, and M1d made the answering burst louder by
    construction — so an unguarded vocabulary score is exactly
    where a spurious gain would land.
  one of eight, nearest centroid on held-out trials: 0.371 (chance 0.125)

  A pairwise table saying every pair is separable does NOT say a word
  can be picked out of eight — that needs every boundary to hold at once.
  The gap between the two numbers above is the interesting part.

  THE VOCABULARY IS FULL BELOW EIGHT — 15 of 28 pairs are under 0.75
  (worst 0.569 against a chance of 0.5), and one of eight reads 0.371
  against a chance of 0.125. Four words hold apart on every pair; eight
  do not, and the hardest rows above say where it runs out.
[exit 1]
